WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.443 --> 00:00:05.668
(Zac screaming into pillow)

00:00:05.668 --> 00:00:08.668
(heavy metal music)

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.890
- Yeah, that's an accurate response.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.690
- Welcome to "Things You Missed."

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.790
We sure wish we missed this one.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.500
Jimmy, how did this all come together?

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.520
- The first title they came up

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.020
with was "Halloween: The Homecoming."

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.220
But the producers switched it,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.470
because after "Halloween: H20's" ending,

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.570
they were nervous people
would only show up

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.720
if they knew for a fact
Michael Myers was back to life.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.890
The director of "Halloween II"

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.060
was brought back for this one,

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.740
but he was actually the third choice

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:35.850
after Whitney Ransick,

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.370
who I personally, unfortunately,
have never heard of,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.842
sorry if they're like huge
director or something like that,

00:00:40.842 --> 00:00:42.420
(gentle music)

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.360
and Dwight H. Little, the
director of "Halloween 4,"

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.370
who I really would've
liked to see come back.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.530
I think he deserved a
second shot at "Halloween."

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.700
But neither of them wanted to,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.170
so they went with Rick Rosenthal.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.150
- Ah, yes, our old friend, Rick.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.580
Not Rick Moranis, not Ric Ocasek,

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.320
hell, not even Rick Astley,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.800
Rick Rosenthal, the director
of "Halloween II" from 1981.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.900
Rick was put in a pretty
tough spot to be fair.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.240
Retconning the end of "H20"
by saying that Michael Myers

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.670
wasn't the one who got killed
was never gonna be popular.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.800
And killing off Laurie Strode
in the first 10 minutes

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.500
is maybe even a bigger slap
in the audience's face.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.670
- But remember, while old Rick

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.380
might be the one who delivered that slap,

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.600
his hand was guided by Malek Akkad.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.480
So given the hand he was
dealt, did he do an okay job?

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.860
- Not even remotely.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.340
Let's get into the "Things
You Missed," before I puke.

