00:01:43.712 --> 00:01:44.851
(air whooshing)

00:01:44.851 --> 00:01:47.934
(eerie upbeat music)

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.820
The film begins with Laurie Strode

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.920
locked away in a sanitarium
after going crazy,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.000
after killing a paramedic

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.620
whom she believed to be Michael Myers.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.510
As much as we're gonna crap on this movie.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.090
- And believe us, we are
going to crap on this movie.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.770
- You have to give it a tiny bit of credit

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.170
for introducing some ideas
that were used years later

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.400
in "Halloween," 2018,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.500
and "Halloween Kills"
in a much better way.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.870
- Both "Resurrection"
and "2018" used the idea

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.640
of Laurie being the crazy one now,

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.800
and in "Resurrection,"
they take it even farther

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.170
by putting her in the
sanitarium instead of Michael.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.790
The established roles are reversed,

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.770
she's even gone mute in this one.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.600
- [Welles] She hasn't
said a word in years,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.000
extreme dissociative disorder.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.520
Now all she does it stare out that window.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.080
- Coincidentally, staring out the window

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.937
is just what Michael
does in the Myers' house

00:02:29.937 --> 00:02:31.320
in "Halloween Kills."

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.910
Laurie is just like Mike.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.740
- Not to be confused with "Like Mike,"

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.480
which also came out in 2002,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.790
and from what I remember,
was a much better movie.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.100
The intro also features Laurie
setting a trap for Michael,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.260
something that's used
later in "Halloween," 2018,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.060
and this very specific scenario

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.650
of someone getting
injured on the staircase

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.390
in the Myers' house with
Michael about to strike,

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.040
before getting distracted and drawn away

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.420
by another potential victim.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.130
This exact circumstance is seen again

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.750
later in "Halloween Kills."

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.070
There's even a line early on,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.890
likening Michael Myers
to a great white shark.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.070
- He's the great white
shark of our unconscious.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.270
- I'll talk about this more in depth

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.350
in a future horror history,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.420
but the filmmakers actually
used "Jaws" as a template

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.030
for Michael Myers in the 40-year trilogy.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:09.960
- [Nelson] And it ended up being

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.710
this very strange mannequin-like,
you know, soulless,

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.714
almost great white shark of a human.

00:03:15.714 --> 00:03:18.270
(intense music)

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.103
- Love that guy.

00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:20.190
Oh, and don't forget that Laurie

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.540
is the one dropped from the rooftop

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.740
during the intro sequence,

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.020
just like she was in "Halloween," 2018,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.610
which is a reversal of what happens

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.780
in the original "Halloween,"

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.370
where Michael is the one who falls

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.320
and feels the relentless pull of gravity.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.420
- We first meet Laurie in
her cell at the sanitarium,

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.590
and she's got this rag doll,

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.380
similar to the doll seen in
her room way back in 1978.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.610
Later on, the same doll is seen

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.530
on the desk of our
protagonist, Sara Moyer,

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.390
perhaps this was old
Rick's way of telling us

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.370
that Sara is the new protagonist now.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.320
- The interesting thing
I learned back in 2018,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:47.430
when I reviewed this movie,

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.380
is that the lead actress, Bianca Kajlich,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.700
actually can't scream.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.980
So every time you hear
her scream in this movie,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.810
it's dubbed, and that gets even weirder

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.280
when you consider that the whole reason

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.230
she's in the Myers'
house in the first place

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.780
is because she's supposedly
the ultimate screen queen.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.160
It's kind of weird, but ultimately,

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.140
it's like the least of
this movie's problems.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.090
- The perfect introduction
to the level of care

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.550
put into this movie can be
observed in these two nurses,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.460
Phillips and Welles, that's W-E-L-L-E-S,

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.560
even though it's spelled
differently in the end credits.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.970
To be fair, "Halloween" 1 and 2

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.440
also had errors in the end credits

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.210
stating that Michael
Myers was 23 years old,

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.230
rather than 21.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.450
Another patient at the
sanitarium is named Harold,

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.270
who is more true crime
obsessed than my mom.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.800
We first see him hiding behind this tree

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.450
as the security guard patrols the grounds,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.220
maybe the only intentionally creepy moment

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.690
that the movie has to offer.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:31.860
He's wearing a clown costume,

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.900
which brings memories of the
original "Halloween" opening,

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.760
where Michael Myers sported
a clown suit of his own.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.890
But he's actually dressed
as John Wayne Gacy,

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.510
a fellow Illinois-born serial criminal,

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.610
who performed as a clown
for children's events.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.960
- He means fellow to Michael Myers,

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.160
not fellow to himself.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.690
Right, Zac?
- No comment.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.850
Like Michael, most of Gacy's
victims were teenagers

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.800
ranging an age from 14 to 21.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.120
Being old Rick's first foray

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.927
into the "Halloween"
franchise in 21 years,

00:04:52.927 --> 00:04:55.320
"Resurrection" has a lot of
callbacks to "Halloween II,"

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.670
whether it be the shot of the night guard

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.380
locating Michael on the security monitors,

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.030
the opening taking place in the hospital,

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.100
or even this scene where a
character slips and falls

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.960
in a puddle of red arterial fluid.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.130
We saw the medic, Jimmy,

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.110
do just that back in the second movie.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.300
- Literally every time
you say that, I look over,

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.860
you'd think I'd be used to that by now.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.810
- Yeah, this is your eighth
time being on this channel,

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.640
which means this is going
to be the sixth time

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.800
that we talk about
"Halloween's" white sheet motif,

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.330
'cause it's not in "Halloween" 3 or 4.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.830
- Michael appearing behind bedsheets

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.690
sort of became a meme
after the first movie

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.370
and plenty of the sequels took note.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.450
In "Halloween Resurrection,"

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.500
the security guard, Willie,

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.820
investigates the laundry room

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.650
where we see a basket of bedsheets.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.300
And then, a minute later he discovers

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.250
his partner's blood in
the laundry machine,

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.590
which is similar to "Halloween
6" where John Strode,

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.630
the most hateable
character in the franchise,

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.370
goes into the basement of his house

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.720
and finds the aftermath

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.090
of his wife's encounter
with Michael Myers.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.640
I did not mean for that to
sound as dirty as it did.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.650
- We first meet our main
character, Sara Moyer,

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.390
in the middle of one
of her college classes.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.980
Yeah, Haddonfield University is back

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.060
after its first appearance

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.650
in "Halloween: The
Curse of Michael Myers,"

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.660
and the professor is a
cameo from none other

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.890
than old Rick himself.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.720
His character's name is Dr. Mixter.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.150
- Dr. Mixter's class, I'm
taking that course too.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.010
- Which was the name of the
head physician at the hospital

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.690
back in Rick's "Halloween II."

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:04.523
Can we call it that?

00:06:04.523 --> 00:06:06.390
- I mean, people call the 2009 entry

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.800
Rob Zombie's "Halloween II,"

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.420
so I don't really see a problem with it.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.760
He's also giving a lesson on
the collective unconscious,

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.370
which is the main theme
explored in "Halloween II,"

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.960
where Laurie's relationship to Michael

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.600
is buried deep within
her unconscious mind.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.830
If you wanna know more about that,

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.210
we actually talked a lot about it

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.860
in the "Halloween II" "Things You Missed."

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:25.080
- Our Rick's "Halloween
II" "Things You Missed."

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.180
- Exactly, after class,
Jen and her friends

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.110
scootered through campus

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.360
where you can see a poster
for a Halloween dance.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.890
This is probably a different dance

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.660
than the one Laurie and Annie made plans

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.040
for in the original "Halloween,"

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.450
'cause that was for a high school dance

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.460
and these posters are on a college campus.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.290
But it still brings back
memories of the original

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.067
and eventually "Halloween," 2018.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:44.310
- "Halloween Resurrection" is
all about this reality show

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.330
called "Dangertainment,"

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.860
which planned to send six college students

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.990
to investigate the Myers'
house on Halloween night.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.220
With the contestants selected,

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.890
the fun, or lack thereof,
would soon begin,

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.114
and as always, it would contained
a few "Things You Missed."

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:58.781
(intense music)

00:07:01.094 --> 00:07:04.177
(eerie upbeat music)

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.230
The producer of
"Dangertainment" is this guy,

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.450
Freddie, whose interests
include saying profanity

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.250
and watching old Kung Fu movies.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:12.840
The latter is a foreshadowing
for his character

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:16.143
who would use martial arts
to attack Michael Myers.

00:07:16.143 --> 00:07:17.430
- Agh!

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.050
- To get ready for the
"Dangertainment" shoot,

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:20.820
Sara and Jen shop for
clothes in a boutique

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:21.750
next to a grocery store

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.210
which proudly displays
a "Dracula 2000" poster.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.590
I've never seen a supermarket

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.760
promoting a horror movie before,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:27.960
so it's obvious that this is here

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.270
because "Resurrection" is
made by Dimension Films,

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.920
who also made "Dracula 2000."

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.900
We saw Dimension trying to
promote their other properties

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:35.137
in the last two "Halloween" movies,

00:07:35.137 --> 00:07:37.170
"The Curse of Michael Myers" and "H20."

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.760
Dimension is also owned by Miramax,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.250
who released the 1994
classic "Pulp Fiction,"

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.380
which could explain why college
students Myles and Scott

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.910
dress up his characters
from "Pulp Fiction"

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:45.870
for a costume party.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.760
I can't think of any
other significant reason

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:48.840
for this reference, can you?

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.060
- No, that makes sense because
"Pulp Fiction" is awesome.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.237
And also, I just remembered,

00:07:52.237 --> 00:07:54.870
"Superbad" follows the same
structure as "Pulp Fiction,"

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.070
and I think that's what makes it

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:57.390
the best comedy of all time.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.760
- Also, when Sara is browsing
costumes with her classmates,

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.770
she briefly sees Michael
Myers in a reflection,

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.050
but turns immediately
to find some random kid.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.670
This moment is never explained.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.320
The only thing I can figure is that Sara

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.180
had expressed thoughts about
dropping out of the show

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.830
due to being too freaked out to sleep.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.660
Maybe she started having hallucinations

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.860
of Michael Myers as well.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:14.790
Whatever the case may be,

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:15.840
the scene is a big callback

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.820
to "Halloween 4: The
Return of Michael Myers,"

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.100
where Jamie Lloyd similarly
sees the boogieman in a mirror

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.525
while browsing costumes and freaks out.

00:08:22.525 --> 00:08:24.180
(Jamie screaming)

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.320
Michael's boutique store visit

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:26.550
isn't the only appearance of his

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.560
that goes completely
unexplained in the movie.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.060
When "Dangertainment" contestant Bill

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:31.380
sneaks up on Jen to scare her,

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.420
the camera glitches out
for no apparent reason,

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.940
and during which we see
one frame of Michael Myers.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.950
None of them have encountered
Michael yet at this point,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.060
so it's not like this is supposed

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.350
to be a "Cloverfield" like effect

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.120
where we're seeing
previously recorded footage.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.170
You could say that this was more

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:44.400
of a "Malignant" type of thing,

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.770
where Michael found a way to
telepathically communicate

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.240
through audio and video devices.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:49.560
But again, that's not something

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:50.703
that ever happens in this movie.

00:08:50.703 --> 00:08:52.530
This same kind of thing happens again

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.430
at the end of the movie,

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:55.020
but this time on the news cameras,

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.310
which makes even less sense,

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:57.450
because they weren't even there

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.040
for anything that happened in the house.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:01.050
The sad thing is I actually
really like the idea

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.490
of a found footage "Halloween" movie.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:03.780
The franchise is so stale

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:05.910
and I think approaching Michael
Myers through found footage

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.400
could be a great way to make
him scary and mysterious again.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.287
But this ain't it, Rick, this ain't it.

00:09:11.287 --> 00:09:12.900
- "Friday the 13th" almost came back

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.570
as a found footage movie
after the 2009 reboot.

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.950
But for a variety of reasons,

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.350
that version of the movie
never got off the ground,

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:21.030
and still all these years later,

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.530
I really would like to see it.

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.420
- As Freddy's assistant,
Nora, gets ready for the show,

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:25.590
she gets up to grab coffee

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.030
while dancing to a song she knows.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:28.560
The camera tilted down to her ass,

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.393
and then back up,

00:09:29.393 --> 00:09:30.870
so we can see what she's actually doing

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.400
is one of the most blatantly forced

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.960
eye-candy moments I've ever seen.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.820
They easily could have
just used a different lens

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:37.050
to get some booty in frame.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.630
But no, our boy Rick was
down bad on this one.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.830
Nora also calls a tow truck

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.540
to remove a car parked
in front of the house.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.550
Given the level of care
put into this movie,

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:47.610
I'm sure the fact that the
license plate says 6395

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:48.990
bears no real significance.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.970
But as someone who was
always on the lookout

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.200
for Easter eggs and secrets,

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.760
my initial thought was
that these were the years

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:55.740
that the initial "Halloween"
timeline took place.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.870
It started when Michael was a kid in 1963

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:58.800
and ended when Michael

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:03.240
confronted Loomis for the
final time in 1995, 63 and 95.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.700
- Coincidence, I think.
- Yes!

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.800
- Besides, none of the other
license plates in the film

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:09.270
seemed to reference anything notable.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:10.950
The characters split
off into three groups.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.540
And, of course, we
followed the two characters

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.430
who weren't even in the
movie before this point,

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:15.870
save for one quick soundbite.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.610
So why would we care
what happened to them?

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.830
There's definitely some
flirtation going on between them,

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.780
but the girl, Donna,
has a comeback that cuts

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:24.630
even deeper than Michael Myers' knife.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:27.090
- Besides, screwing a music major

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:29.010
would be tantamount to lesbianism.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.390
- I'm pretty sure John Carpenter,

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.950
the director of the original "Halloween,"

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.200
was a music major at
Western Kentucky University

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.210
before transferring to USC to study film.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.640
So that line is either a really funny jab

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.770
or a painfully awkward mistake.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:42.180
- I don't know the exact relationship

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.650
between Rosenthal and Carpenter,

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.210
but based on what Carpenter has said

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.800
about "Halloween II" over the years,

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.660
I would guess this line is intentional.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:49.890
Speaking of "Halloween I,"

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.480
Sara finds herself in a situation

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:54.030
that's very comparable to
what happens to Laurie Strode.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.650
She investigates a shuttered closet

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.570
and gets scared by a
dummy that falls on her.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:58.403
Her friend Rudy,

00:10:58.403 --> 00:11:00.030
instead of simply opening the closet,

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.800
just punches his hands
straight through it,

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.200
which is obviously reminiscent
of what Michael does

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.060
when Laurie is the one
trapped in the closet

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.560
at the end of "Halloween I."

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.880
This is what we call a dumb Easter egg.

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.010
Not only does it not add
anything to the movie,

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.980
but everyone who just saw it
is dumber after witnessing it.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.990
Down in the basement,
donna is scared by a rat,

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.160
which is something that happens

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.080
in the only other movie in this franchise

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.007
where the Myers' house is
shown to have a basement,

00:11:21.007 --> 00:11:23.310
"Halloween 5: The Revenge
of Michael Myers."

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.500
Basically, if you see a
Myers' house with a basement,

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.390
you can assume you're in for a bad time.

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:28.800
Donna later discovers that Michael

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.020
has been surviving in the
basement by eating rats,

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.880
and that's a callback
to the original movie

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.020
when Brackett and Loomis

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.270
discover the half-eaten
dog in the Myers' house.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.590
- It is also in this basement

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.960
where she stumbles upon this
article about Laurie Strode.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.250
I guess this is supposed to tell us

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.620
that Michael has been keeping
tabs on her all this time,

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.510
which we already knew from "H20,"

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.680
and we don't really need to know

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:47.970
because Laurie's already dead.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.870
Donna reads out the supposed headline.

00:11:50.827 --> 00:11:53.940
- [Donna] "Laurie Strode,
sister of Michael Myers,

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.550
survives Halloween night massacre."

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.837
- Which doesn't match what
the text actually says.

00:11:58.837 --> 00:12:01.380
"Laurie Strode has been nominated
by the Chamber of Commerce

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.510
as the most commonly," something "teen."

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:04.860
I can't make out what that word is.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.570
I spent like 10 minutes
trying to figure it out

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:08.400
and was not willing to
waste any more of my life

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:11.040
with a minute detail from
the worst "Halloween" movie.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.600
- Zac and I took a super close look

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.280
and we both think it says, "Spirited,"

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.200
but, "the most commonly spirited teen"

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.430
doesn't really make sense.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.200
So I don't really know or care.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.150
It's just weird, and we
wanted to point it out.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:23.400
- The picture chosen for the
article is interesting though.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.080
It's actually this behind-the-scenes photo

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.090
taken during the production
of the original "Halloween,"

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.230
and during the scene where Laurie waits

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:30.270
for a pick-up from Annie
right outside her house.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.190
If anyone wants to make their
own version of this photo,

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.600
you can still go to the location,

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.730
and they even leave a
pumpkin out to use as a prop.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.160
- Donna nearly hooks up with
her fellow contestant, Jim.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.500
Yes, another Jim in the
"Halloween" universe.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.030
It's getting old at this point.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.500
Which, by the way, is really stupid,

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.660
because the whole reason
they're there is to be filmed

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.010
and they know they're on camera,

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.270
so why wouldn't you just wait

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.770
till after the show to hook up?

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.030
After this, Donna gets dressed

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:52.230
and explores the basement more,

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:54.330
which is when she has her
encounter with Michael Myers.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.670
He kills her by impaling
her on this crooked beam

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:57.840
that's sticking out of the gate,

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:00.450
during which she is somehow
magically wearing a bra again,

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.283
which is weird,

00:13:01.283 --> 00:13:03.330
because earlier we saw
her put her shirt back on

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.580
and she's very clearly not wearing a bra.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.680
I just can't believe Rick
would let this slide.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.780
- Once the bloodshed
begins, it doesn't stop.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:12.030
But if we take a closer
look at some of these kills,

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:14.300
we can find a few more anomalies.

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:17.217
(thunder rattling)

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:21.720
(eerie music)

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.780
Another "Halloween" franchise trope

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:25.830
that happens in this movie

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:28.020
is the one where someone is
mistaken for Michael Myers

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:29.370
and pays the price for it.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.200
The first time we saw
this was with Ben Tramer

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.970
in Rick's "Halloween II," RIP,

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.145
then Ted Hollister in "Halloween 4."

00:13:35.145 --> 00:13:38.760
(slow violin music)

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.320
Then, Spitz in "Halloween 5."

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.270
In "Halloween Resurrection,"
it's the producer, Freddie.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.400
We can actually see the
Michael Myers mask on his desk

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.720
before he goes into the house with it

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.890
and gets attacked by Jim.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.650
Unlike Ben, and Ted, and
Spitz, Freddie survives.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.540
Sara's friend Jen is not so lucky.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.420
She gets decapitated by the
real Michael Myers, not you,

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:56.700
after which we can see the
inside of the mannequin's neck.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.170
They didn't add any visual effects here

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.070
to make it look real.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.810
I normally don't mind cheesy effects

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:01.950
in a low-budget horror movie,

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:02.783
but the problem here

00:14:02.783 --> 00:14:04.650
is that one of the plot
points of this movie

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.600
is literally that the house
is filled with mannequins

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.590
and Halloween decorations

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.540
staged by the "Dangertainment"
production team.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.100
So it's unclear if we're
supposed to believe

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.810
that Jen's death is staged or real,

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.460
which is exactly how the internet viewers

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.840
at the Halloween party react.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.760
Myles thinks it's real
and calls the police

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:18.870
and gets connected immediately,

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.070
because the makers of this movie

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.203
have no idea how a phone call works.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:24.713
- Hello, 911?

00:14:24.713 --> 00:14:26.790
- [Urmaker] This has been real 911 calls

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:27.990
that actually happened.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:30.030
- Rudy is the next character
to confront Michael.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.040
I know his whole character
is him being a chef

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:33.570
and all he thinks about is nutrition,

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:34.980
but I love how that's still the only thing

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:37.383
he talks about as he's
facing certain death.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:39.960
- [Rudy] You should try
a little less protein

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.220
in your diet, you know?

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:42.373
Control some of that aggression, huh?

00:14:42.373 --> 00:14:43.950
- I don't even know if that's a thing.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.990
The only reputable study
I've been able to find

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:48.930
linking protein and
aggression was studying dogs.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.240
- Do you think dogs are
a good source of protein?

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.370
- I don't wanna find out,
but according to this movie,

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.590
rats are a perfectly
fine source of protein.

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:57.720
Rudy gets to be the victim
of the knife pin kill,

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.100
also known as the Bob Simms kill,

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.000
the Kelly Meeker kill,

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.560
the Nurse Mary kill, the Dave kill,

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.580
whatever you wanna call it.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.740
Sara ends up being the
only remaining contestant,

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.420
so Myles, also known as Deckard,

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.410
sends her text messages

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.330
to alert her of Michael's
position in the house.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:10.800
Like this one, where he informs her

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.320
that Michael is in the hallway
and says, "Don't scream,"

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:15.511
to which she immediately screams.

00:15:15.511 --> 00:15:16.344
(Sara screams)

00:15:16.344 --> 00:15:18.930
What a dumbass, she's even
worse than Nina from "Saw 7."

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.150
- Why wouldn't you just
shut the (censored) up?

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.470
- Sara climbs out through the window

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.670
onto the roof to escape,

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:24.870
which might be a callback

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.730
to Rachel and Jamie in "Halloween 4."

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.310
I'm gonna believe it is
because I love "Halloween 4."

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:30.600
I also find it really funny

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.820
that Michael opens the
window by headbutting it.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.900
I guess people in this movie

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:36.330
just really like to break
things instead of opening them.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.940
As we already mentioned, Sara
is just not the brightest.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:40.590
I don't know how she even got accepted

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:41.970
into Haddonfield University,

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.920
because instead of going
to the lowest point

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.180
of the roof and jumping,

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:47.430
she goes back into the house to escape.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.320
You know, the house where
the serial killer is.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:50.820
I mean the roof isn't even that high.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:52.440
It certainly seems safer to jump

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.970
rather than climbing over the body

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:55.410
hanging from the attic stairs.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:56.243
For a moment there,

00:15:56.243 --> 00:15:58.200
it looks like she's about to
Spider-Man kiss the corpse,

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:59.400
which is funny if you consider

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.110
that Spider-Man was still in theaters

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.720
when "Resurrection" came
out in July of 2002.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.610
Freddie comes back to
the house to save Sara

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.560
and drops this line on Michael.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.570
- So you wanna be on "Dangertainment"?

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.250
- Not only is that a terrible line,

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.440
but Michael's reaction
is certainly meme worthy.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:14.640
You're in his house.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.170
Imagine if I broke into someone's house

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.300
to ask them if they wanted
to be on "Things You Missed."

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.640
In true Rick Rosenthal
"Halloween" movie fashion,

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.620
it ends with Michael being lit on fire.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.210
Things get a little bit dicey for Sara

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.760
when she gets pinned
down by, a mixing board?

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:28.080
Are you (censored) serious?

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.220
Anyway, Freddie saves her

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.470
by electrocuting Michael
Myers in the penis,

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.990
which sends him flying
across the room apparently.

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:35.670
It's good to know that
Michael's one weakness

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:37.620
is being electrocuted in the penis.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.540
There are actually four
endings to this movie.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:41.460
One where Michael comes
back to life on the gurney

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.370
and is immediately killed by
an ax that Sara somehow has.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.110
One where she meets Deckard/Myles

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:47.670
in real life and he says...

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.230
- Well, you did it.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.891
You killed the boogeyman.

00:16:50.891 --> 00:16:52.489
(eerie music)

00:16:52.489 --> 00:16:53.940
- You can't kill the boogeyman.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.440
- Which is a callback
to Tommy Doyle's line

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:56.430
in the original movie.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:59.117
- You can't kill the boogeyman.

00:16:59.117 --> 00:16:59.950
(kid screams)

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.560
- And one where crime scene investigators

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:03.870
are let in by this cop, who
is played by Brad Loree,

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.060
the actor under the Michael
Myers mask throughout the movie.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.980
That one ends with Michael
reaching out of the wreckage

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.320
to grab the investigator
as a one last scare moment.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.420
Supposedly, Rick wanted to
send a different versions

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.340
of the film out to different
theaters so that the ending

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.200
you got could have been
any one of these four.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.840
This tactic was used for
the 1985 film "Clue."

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:20.190
I actually think it's a cool idea,

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.480
but the studio rejected it,

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.010
probably realizing that it was a tactic

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:25.950
that would only build hype if
the movie was actually good.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.000
- So the ending scene of the movie

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.070
shows Michael coming back
to life in the morgue,

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.990
which obviously finally gives meaning

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:33.180
to the title of "Halloween Resurrection."

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:34.860
I think that's why they
called it that anyway,

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.540
because there's no other resurrection

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.830
that happens in this movie.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.870
This movie also went through
several different titles

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.770
before it came out.

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:42.630
We already mentioned
"Halloween Homecoming,"

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.490
but there was also "Halloween H2K,"

00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:46.380
which I guess is a riff on Y2K,

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.570
which is kind of weird because
it happened a few years

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:49.770
before this movie came out.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.320
And also, "Halloween: MichaelMyers.com."

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:54.540
Yes, "Halloween: MichaelMyers.com."

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:57.240
Wow, that is one of the
worst titles I've ever heard.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.770
- Ultimately, I find it pretty funny

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.870
that they decided on "Halloween
Resurrection" though.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:03.060
There's something so
ironic about "Resurrection"

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.777
being the one to kill your franchise.

00:18:04.777 --> 00:18:06.390
"Halloween Resurrection" was so bad

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.490
that they decided to
end the 20-year timeline

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:09.960
and start fresh five years later

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.790
with Rob Zombie's remake of "Halloween."

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:12.990
However, we're gonna skip ahead

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:14.970
and talk about the 40-year timeline next.

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.650
So get ready, if you wanna hear everything

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.487
you might have missed
in "Halloween," 2018,

00:18:18.487 --> 00:18:20.820
"Halloween Kills" and "Halloween Ends."

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:23.160
Look out for those new episodes
in the playlist on the left.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.200
Thanks to Jimmy Champane
for joining me once again.

